  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening Institute of Chartered Accountantscomma Sri Lanka</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Background: The Institute of Chartered Accountants in Sri Lanka (ICASL) is the national accountancy body and the sole Accounting Standards setting authority in Sri Lanka. The ICASL also conducts qualifying examinationscomma supervises and regulates student education and trainingcomma secures the maintenance of professional standards among members and the advancement of the profession. The institute has over 4200 memberscomma and over 30comma000 registered students. There was a   recent request to the World Bank by the Government of Sri Lanka  for support of the Institute of Chartered Accounts of Sri Lanka (ICASL) on various corporate governance and public financial management improvements efforts including; -  Enhancing corporate reporting by introducing international financial reporting standards to Strategic Business Enterprises (SBEs). - Enriching the quality of audits by establishing and implementation of an audit quality assurance board and strengthening small and medium practioners. - Improving public sector financial reporting by rolling out a new set of public sector accounting standards. ----------------------------------------------------------------</narrative>
  </description>
